    "narrative": "Our primary offensive engine today features **Corbin Carroll** (74.49) and **Brice Turang** (73.39), who represent our strongest plays. Both benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with high expected ERAs (Woodruff at 3.83 vs **Corbin Carroll**, and Kelly at 5.47 vs **Brice Turang**). **Corbin Carroll** is a priority start due to the 100% stolen base opportunity window against Woodruff, which aligns perfectly with our need to aggressively chase SB volume. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (71.12) is locked in against a struggling Bieber; the 19% boost from the SP skill profile makes him a premier anchor for our middle-of-the-order production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Cole Young** (50.21) on the bench. He was the final cut, narrowly missing the utility slot because his projected efficiency\u2014dampened by a negative park factor\u2014fell just short of the high-floor versatility offered by **Zach McKinstry** and **Alex Freeland**. While **Cole Young** remains a viable depth piece, we prioritized the speed-heavy profiles of our starting outfielders today. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Henry Bolte**. Should any of these players move down the order or get squeezed out of the lineup entirely, the efficiency score will shift, potentially opening a path for **Austin Riley** or **Isaac Paredes** to move off the bench.\n\nA final word of caution: while **James Wood** brings an elite xwOBA of 0.418, his score of 52.66 is constrained by the tough 3.19 xERA of Ashcraft. We are betting on **James Wood**\u2019s raw talent and top-of-the-order position to overcome the SP matchup. Conversely, **Mickey Moniak** (69.72) and **Kyle Karros** (63.92) enjoy a massive +14% park factor boost that helps mitigate the risks associated with facing Robbie Ray. We remain wary of the Catcher efficiency drop-off for our catchers\u2014**Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**\u2014as we are facing several elite defensive backstops today that may stifle our aggressive base-running strategy.",
